    <title lang="en">Yi Dai Jiang Shi</title>
    <desc lang="en">Set in the pivotal year of 1911—the eve of the Xinhai Revolution—Yi Dai Jiang Shi focuses on "Liuhe Hall," a renowned woodcarving studio in Putian, Fujian. Celebrated for their peerless "Xianzuo" (??) carving style, the Liao family has enjoyed imperial favor for generations. However, behind the workshop's prestigious facade lies a family vulnerable to changing times and deep-seated rivalries.</desc>
